    {
      "ordinal": 6,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.2",
      "title": "Transitional Style Helmets",
      "body": "● In the middle of the 14th century, bascinets with a side-hinged visor began to be depicted in miniatures and art. They include a longer visor with no chin plate (such as sugarloaf) and will represent the majority of helmets until the middle of the 15th century.\n● Transitional style helmets are approved for 14th-century and transitional armor.\n● Transitional style helmets are denied for 15th-century armor.",
      "page_from": 5,
      "page_to": 5,
