      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.3",
      "title": "15th-century Style Helmets",
      "body": "At the edge of the 15th century, an evolution of previous bascinets was developed. The great bascinet encompasses an increased neck protection that makes it very safe. Some extant artifacts are displayed in museums.\n\nA   B   C\n\nA: Musée de l’Armée, Paris - 1400/1420 - France B: Musées des Beaux Arts, Dijon - 1400/1420 - France C: Doges Palace, Venice - 1380/1390 - Italy",
