    {
      "ordinal": 12,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "Visor requirements",
      "body": "● The visor must not be too long or too short, it must conform to the proportions of historical sources.\n● The hinges must be reproduced as per historical sources.\n● It is permitted to weld the visor down. A welded visor must resemble a functional removable visor.\n● It is permitted to add metal plates to protect the throat. Such a plate must be strong enough to endure full-contact fighting and must be concealed under the aventail.\n● A leather strap can be used to secure the visor.\n● Breath holes should be round and must not exceed a diameter of 10mm. Breath holes must not be so numerous that they compromise the helm’s structural integrity. It is acceptable to mirror breath holes to both sides.\n● Breath holes of other shapes must be documented by historical sources to be permitted.",
      "page_from": 8,
      "page_to": 8,
      "stable_key": "side-pivoting-visored-bascinets:3.2",
      "parent_key": "side-pivoting-visored-bascinets:3",
